function isPalindrome(s) {
  const clean = s.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '');
  let left = 0, right = clean.length - 1;
  while (left < right) {
    if (clean[left] !== clean[right]) return false;
    left++;
    right--;
  }
  return true;
}
```

Same idea as the Python version: lowercase, strip anything that isn't a letter or digit with a regex, then walk two pointers inward and return false on the first mismatch. Time O(n), space O(n) for the cleaned string.

